# Populate this manifest with the SHA-256 of each Oracle installer zip
# before running `vagrant up`. The guest-side provisioner verifies the SHA-256
# against these entries before extracting the zip into GI_HOME / DB_HOME.
#
# Example:
#   sha256sum ORCL_software/LINUX.X64_213000_grid_home.zip
#   sha256sum ORCL_software/LINUX.X64_213000_db_home.zip
#
# Then copy the output here, replacing the example path with /vagrant/...
# Expected filenames:
#   /vagrant/LINUX.X64_213000_grid_home.zip
#   /vagrant/LINUX.X64_213000_db_home.zip
#
# A Release Update is optional. If you set env.opatch_software and
# env.gi_ru_software in config/vagrant.yml, add an entry for each of those
# zips here too, e.g.:
#   sha256sum ORCL_software/p6880880_210000_Linux-x86-64.zip
# Expected filenames:
#   /vagrant/p6880880_210000_Linux-x86-64.zip
#   /vagrant/p<bug-number>_210000_Linux-x86-64.zip
#
# Format (one entry per line):
#   <sha256>  /vagrant/<installer-zip>
c05d5c32a72b9bf84ab6babb49aee99cbb403930406aabe3cf2f94f1d35e0916  /vagrant/LINUX.X64_213000_db_home.zip
070d4471bc067b1290bdcee6b1c1fff2f21329d2839301e334bcb2a3d12353a3  /vagrant/LINUX.X64_213000_grid_home.zip
